AcCountDeer uses a straightforward accounting approach to support deer population management and harvest-related decisions. The model (spreadsheet model also available) is designed to be transparent, flexible, and accessible, with underlying assumptions, parameters, and processes that are readily understandable to wildlife managers. By integrating routinely available population and harvest data, AcCountDeer provides a practical tool for evaluating harvest-management scenarios and projecting population trend so informed harvest regulations can be made. This tool was originally developed for white-tailed deer (Odocoileus virginianus) but is readily adaptable to model populations of other species of the Cervidae family.
}
\details{
The model outputs describe the population composition at three separate snapshots in time (postharvest, mid-year, and preharvest) as well as the annual harvest projections of each sex-age class. Further descriptions of population snapshots are as follows: Postharvest: Snapshot after harvest season; Mid-Year: Snapshot during fawning season; Preharvest: Snapshot before harvest season; Harvest Projection: Projected yields for each sex-age class
}
